                  "explanation": "Weiss's two primary fee-raise triggers are oversubscription (you have more demand than supply, so the market is telling you to charge more) and the 24-month rule (no raise in 2 years = falling behind inflation and your own growth). Client pushback signals price-sensitivity, not under-pricing; losing a deal to a higher-priced competitor is rare and not a reliable trigger; formal credentials matter less than thought-leadership credentials (books, speeches, notable wins). The trigger discipline is what produces the 2-3x lifetime revenue advantage.",
